# Save feedback (accounting sandbox)

## Invariant

Every explicit **Save** (or Post / Save snapshot) must give the user a **visible confirmation or error** they can notice without opening DevTools. Silent success feels like “nothing happened.”

## Correct pattern

1. User clicks Save → loading state on button optional (`Saving…`).
2. On success → **banner and/or button label** within the same viewport as the button (not only at the top of a long form).
3. Clear after ~2–4s, or keep until next edit.
4. On failure → red/error message in the same place.
5. Profile / settings forms: **Save is the commit** (draft toggles do not replace the success message).

Preferred UX (pick one or combine):

| Pattern | Example in repo |
|---------|-----------------|
| Green/blue banner beside or just above the Save row | `ApiKeyForm`, lodgment `snapshotMessage` |
| Button text flips to **Saved!** briefly | `TaxReportingForm` in SettingsPage, `FyStartPreferencesEditor` |
| Inline status line under the control | ABA `message`, worksheets `message` |

## Audit (Settings + common Save)

| Location | Save control | Feedback today | Notes |
|----------|--------------|----------------|-------|
| `BusinessProfileForm` | Save | Banner **at form top** only | Easy to miss after scrolling to GST / Save at bottom — must also show **next to Save** |
| `ApiKeyForm` | Save | Banner above buttons | OK |
| `TaxReportingForm` (SettingsPage) | Save Tax & Reporting | Button → Saved! | OK |
| `FyStartPreferencesEditor` | Save starting quarter | Button label | OK |
| `PAYGConfigForm` | enable/disable flows | Banner when `isSaved` | OK when path sets it |
| `DirectorsLoanSettingsForm` | Save ×2 | **None** | Gap — add brief Saved / error |
| `RemittanceAndAbaPanel` | Save ABA settings | `message` | OK |
| `ManualJournalPanel` | Post journal | `success` / `error` | OK |
| `TaxWorksheetsPanel` | Save worksheets | `message` | OK if rendered near button |
| `ATOLodgmentGuide` / Individual | Save snapshot | `snapshotMessage` | OK |
| Transaction History date/amount | check icons | Inline | OK (not a form Save) |
| Cash expense | onSave | dashboard toast / expand | Prefer explicit success string |

## Do

- Place success UI **adjacent to the Save button** on long Settings forms.
- Keep English copy (default language).
- Failures must be as visible as success.

## Do not

- Rely only on a banner at the **top** of a scrolled form.
- Treat console.log as user feedback.
- Auto-save critical settings without any confirmation when a Save button exists (see GST Registered → Save commit model).
